    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math practice by adapting to individual learning paces and styles. They can generate relevant problems, explain concepts in simple terms, and provide instant feedback. This helps students build confidence and see math as a tool for real-world applications, not just abstract theory."
